  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "tap-protocolinfo: minor memory management tweaks",
  "description": "Add a finish function to the call of `register_tap_listener()` which\nfrees the memory allocated by the tap. This is just the tap data which\nis allocated when the listener is registered.\n\nWhen registering the listener, free our copy of the filter string.\n`register_tap_listener()` takes its own copy of it, so we're leaking our\ncopy if we don't free it.\n\nWhen registering the listener, replace two-stage\n`g_malloc()`+`g_strlcpy()` with a single call to `g_strndup()`. Note the\nminor semantic difference between the two: [`g_strlcpy()`][CPY] copies\n\"At most `dest_size`-1 characters\" whereas [`g_strndup()`][DUP] copies\n\"the first `n` bytes of a string\". (Both guarantee a null terminator on\nthe new copy.)\n\n[CPY]: https://docs.gtk.org/glib/func.strlcpy.html\n[DUP]: https://docs.gtk.org/glib/func.strndup.html\n\nPing #20432",
